      "writtenOn": "2018-10-29T16:22:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it is generally useful to have at least one use of a new API to help review the API, but if it\u0027s better to separate them I\u0027m ok with that.\n\nThe ones left in the \"old way\" are:\n1) the ones related to buffer pointer objects and fixups which required more refactoring that justified a separate patch\n2) reading a local copy of binder objects which gets its own new function -- also seemed like it would be better in its own patch.\n\nWhich cases do you think would be best to bring into this patch? Or would it be better to introduce all the APIs together and then all the uses of those APIs together?",
